# WORLD — state of play, end of 2026-08-22 session

Page 1 of the new document is an old-game world map: a PATH through the four companies, each
with an arrow above it pointing up to its label (`XTIX — BUILT FROM ZERO`). This file is the
handoff. It records what exists, what is honestly wrong with it, and the ordered plan to fix
it — enough to resume cold without re-deriving anything.

Read with: `ARCHITECTURE.md` (the contract), `DECISIONS.md` (why), `KIT_OPTIONS.md` (D1–D27).

---

## 1. Where the files are

| What | Path |
|---|---|
| Generator (authored blueprints → binary blob) | `world-build/tools/world3_gen.py` |
| Viewer (WebGL2 instanced renderer → one HTML) | `world-build/tools/world2_view.py` |
| Model index, 824 models across 11 kits | `world-build/kits/all/index.json` |
| Raw-bbox measuring tool | `world-build/tools/measure.py` |
| Built page (4.7 MB, base64 blob inline) | `repo/lab/world.html` |
| Local server (also accepts frames back) | `world-build/tools/serve.py` — port 8732 |
| Label compositor (pins are DOM, not canvas) | `world-build/tools/pinlabel.py` |
| **Headless renderer — works with the screen locked** | `world-build/tools/shoot.py` |

Rebuild and view:

```bash
cd "C:/Users/Alex/Desktop/Oran_Personal_Brand/world-build/tools" && python world3_gen.py && python world2_view.py
```

Everything lives in `Oran_Personal_Brand/world-build/` — deliberately outside the repo, since
31 MB of source models are build inputs, not site output. It is **not** in the scratchpad any
more; that folder is wiped at the end of a session.

To view interactively, run `serve.py` and open `http://127.0.0.1:8732/lab/world.html`. In the
console, `__cam(yaw,pitch,dist,tx,tz)` frames it and `__shot('name.png')` POSTs the canvas to
`world-build/shots/`. For unattended work use `shoot.py` instead — see below.

**Whole-map framing used for the review shot:** `__cam(-0.79, 0.72, 80, 0.5, -1.5)` at a
1600×1000 viewport.

### Rendering without a display

`shoot.py` is the one that matters for unattended work. The interactive browser cannot
screenshot a pane that is not being shown — an occluded window stops compositing frames — so
every render step died the moment the screen was locked. Headless Chrome with SwiftShader
rasterises WebGL2 in software: no GPU, no display, no unlocked desktop.

```bash
python world-build/tools/shoot.py all
```

7-11 s per 1600x1000 frame for the full 266,805-triangle world, and it captures the whole
**page**, so the DOM labels and arrows are included. The viewer takes its camera from the URL
(`world.html?clean#yaw,pitch,dist,tx,tz`), so a frame needs no console and no interaction.

Measured power settings on this machine: on AC, `STANDBYIDLE = 0` and `HIBERNATEIDLE = 0` —
it never sleeps, so a locked screen does not interrupt a build. On battery it sleeps after
**20 minutes**, which does. Long unattended runs must be on mains.

---

## 2. What the current build actually contains

Reported by the renderer: **104 distinct models · 6,337 instances · 266,805 drawn triangles**,
on a 46 × 34 tile grid where 1 tile = 8 m.

Composed, not scattered — this was the fix for the previous rejection:

- **93 groves (656 trees).** A grove picks ONE dominant species and clusters around a centre.
  A tree that would land alone in open ground is not placed at all.
- **16 avenue trees** in even rows along both sides of the road either side of OASIS — the
  visible difference between land that grew and land somebody arranged.
- **96 riparian** plants crowding the river bank and thinning inland.
- **265 undergrowth** props, only where there is forest to be under.
- **The land rises** from XTIX to MEDCOIN; **the forest thins** along the same line. Elevation
  is the career, not decoration.
- The route surface changes with the story: **dirt track** where nothing is built yet, **made
  road** once there is a settlement to serve.

---

## 3. Honest verdict on the current build

Shown to Oran as `v5_MAP_labelled.png`. **Not at reference level. Do not ship it.**

What works, and should be kept:

1. **OASIS reads as a settlement.** Houses *face* a square, with fences, front paths, planters,
   a market row and people. This is the one place that works, and it works because it was
   authored tile by tile. It is the template for the other three.
2. **The groves read as forest**, not scatter. The rule earned that.
3. **The road reads as a road** — proper tiles, markings, autotiled corners.
4. **The four arrows and labels are correct** and land above their places.

What is wrong, in severity order:

| # | Problem | Cause |
|---|---|---|
| **W1** | **XTIX is invisible.** From the map view it is a few green specks in the trees. It reads as scattered debris, not BUILT FROM ZERO. | Its blueprint is all survival-kit ground clutter — tools, crates, a bedroll. Zero vertical mass. At 8 m per tile a workbench is correctly ~¼ tile, so realistic scale is exactly what makes it vanish. |
| **W2** | **MEDCOIN is one small grey blob.** No presence as a summit. | Only 8 props, and industrial `building-f` is small at this scale. |
| **W3** | **EVENTER is a scatter of blue specks.** The crossing does not cross anything. | The route is a single staircase line, so there is no second road to meet it. ALIGNMENT has nothing to align. |
| **W4** | **The terraces are ugly** — long straight dark-brown rectangular walls chopping the map into arbitrary blocks. | `height()` rounds a smooth field to 0.5 steps, so contours come out straight and long; cliff blocks tint into the **bark** (brown) family and read as wood, not rock; the terrace lip is bare, so nothing breaks the geometry. |
| **W5** | **~70% of the map is undifferentiated forest** with nothing in it. | The four places occupy a tiny fraction of 46 × 34. Either the map shrinks or the places grow. |
| **W6** | **Everything is one dark green.** Low contrast, no light direction, no time of day. | Ground tint jitter is ±14 % per tile, which reads as a visible chequerboard rather than variation. |
| **W7** | **The dirt track is a thin wobbly brown line** — the exact "a path that isn't a path, just a coloured line" criticism from before. | nature-kit `ground_path*` is a narrow track inset in a grass tile. Wrong asset. |
| **W8** | **Road tiles leave gaps** at their edges. | `SCALE['city-kit-roads'] = 0.85` shrinks the tile itself. See §5 — this is a real bug. |
| **W9** | Some props render as near-black silhouettes. | Unconfirmed; suspect degenerate triangles giving garbage normals, or no ambient floor in the shader. |

